ed the failing fragment to be i>0. Let me fix: u1 succeeds, u2 raises DownloadError. i=1, skip_unavailable_fragments=True \u2192 fatal = False or not True = False \u2192 not fatal \u2192 report_skip_fragment(2) \u2192 break. Then count=0 which is not > fragment_retries (0) \u2192 continue loop \u2192 finish \u2192 True.\n\nSo:\n```python\ndef fake_download(ctx, url, info):\n    if url == 'u2':\n        raise DownloadError('boom')\n    return True, b'data'\n```\nskipped == [2], downloaded == ['u1'].\n\nTest 10: resume \u2014 fragment_index set by prepare \u2192 skip first fragment.\n\n```python\ndef test_resume_skips_downloaded_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), {})\n    downloaded = []\n    def fake_prepare(ctx):\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = 1  # first fragment already downloaded\n    ...\n    info = {'fragments': [{'url': 'u1'}, {'url': 'u2'}]}\n    result = fd.real_download('f', info)\n    assert result is True\n    assert downloaded == ['u2']\n```\n\nTrace: frag_index=1 for first fragment: 1 <= 1 \u2192 continue. Second: frag_index=2 > 1 \u2192 download. Good, covers lines 36-37.\n\nTest 11: skip_unavailable_fragments=False with DownloadError on non-first fragment \u2192 fatal \u2192 raise.\n\n```python\ndef test_download_error_no_skip_raises(monkeypatch):\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), {'skip_unavailable_fragments': False})\n    def fake_download(ctx, url, info):\n        if url == 'u2':\n            raise DownloadError('boom')\n        return True, b'data'\n    with pytest.raises(DownloadError):\n        fd.real_download('f', {'fragments': [{'url': 'u1'}, {'url': 'u2'}]})\n```\n\nThis covers the `not skip_unavailable_fragments` part of line 40 and the raise branch at line 69 via non-first fragment.\n\nAlso, maybe test HTTPError exhausted with skip_unavailable_fragments=False on non-first fragment \u2192 fatal \u2192 report_error + return False. That covers line 40's second operand in the count>fragment_retries branch. Let me add:\n\nTest 12: HTTPError exhausted, skip_unavailable_fragments=False, non-first fragment \u2192 report_error, return False.\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_exhausted_no_skip_fatal(monkeypatch):\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), {'fragment_retries': 0, 'skip_unavailable_fragments': False})\n    errors = []\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error', lambda msg: errors.append(msg))\n    def fake_download(ctx, url, info):\n        if url == 'u2':\n            raise compat_urllib_error.HTTPError('http://x', 500, 'Server Error', None, None)\n        return True, b'data'\n    result = fd.real_download('f', {'fragments': [{'url': 'u1'}, {'url': 'u2'}]})\n    assert result is False\n    assert errors == ['giving up after 0 fragment retries']\n```\n\nHmm wait, fragment_retries=0: count=0, while 0<=0: raise \u2192 count=1, 1<=0 false. Exit. count=1 > 0 \u2192 fatal (not skip_unavailable \u2192 True) \u2192 report_error \u2192 return False. Good.\n\nAlso, what about the case where fragment has no 'url' and no fragment_base_url \u2192 assert fails (AssertionError). Line 46: `assert fragment_base_url`. Should I test that? It's a branch (assert). The assert statement itself is line 46; if fragment_url is falsy we execute line 46. If fragment_base_url is truthy, line 47 executes. If falsy, AssertionError. To cover line 46 fully (the assert check), having a fragment without url and with fragment_base_url set executes line 46 (evaluates it) and line 47. The AssertionError branch would also be nice but it's an assert \u2014 coverage-wise, line 46 is covered either way. I could add a test for the AssertionError for completeness:\n\nTest 13: fragment without url and without fragment_base_url \u2192 AssertionError.\n\n```python\ndef test_missing_base_url_asserts(monkeypatch):\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), {})\n    with pytest.raises(AssertionError):\n        fd.real_download('f', {'fragments': [{'path': 'seg'}]})\n```\n\nHmm, but wait \u2014 AssertionError raised inside the try block... The except clauses catch HTTPError and DownloadError. AssertionError propagates. Good.\n\nActually, is it worth it? It does exercise line 46's failing branch. I'll include it \u2014 it's cheap.\n\nNow, about the ydl mock: FileDownloader.__init__ might call things on ydl. Let me check what FileDownloader.__init__ does in youtube_dl:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, ydl, params):\n    \"\"\"Create a FileDownloader object.\"\"\"\n    self.ydl = ydl\n    self._progress_hooks = []\n    self.params = params\n    self._retcode = 0\n    self._interrupted = False\n    self._interrupt_trigger = ...\n```\n\nHmm, I don't remember exactly. Let me check with get_info. Actually, in youtube_dl (the older project), FileDownloader.__init__:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, ydl, params):\n    \"\"\"Create a FileDownloader object.\"\"\"\n    self.ydl = ydl\n    self._progress_hooks = []\n    self.params = params\n    self._last_progress_update = 0\n    self._interrupted = False\n```\n\nSomething like that. It doesn't call ydl methods I think. Actually it might call `self.report_progress`... no. Let me just check.\n\nAlso, `to_screen` in common.py:\n```python\ndef to_screen(self, message, skip_eol=False, check_quiet=False):\n    \"\"\"Print message to stdout if not in quiet mode\"\"\"\n    if self.params.get('logger'):\n        self.params['logger'].debug(message)\n    ...\n    else:\n        self.ydl.to_screen(...)\n```\n\nSince I'm mocking report_* methods in most tests, to_screen won't be called. But in tests where I don't mock report_retry_fragment (e.g., test 6 exhausts retries and calls report_retry_fragment at count=1)... I said I'd mock it. Let me make sure every test mocks all report_* and _* methods that could hit ydl, to be safe. Actually, using a MagicMock ydl means even if real methods are called, they'd work (MagicMock returns MagicMock for anything). But real `to_screen` might do string formatting \u2014 fine with MagicMock.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: FileDownloader.to_screen might check `self.params.get('quiet')`. With params dict lacking 'quiet', it calls self.ydl.to_screen(...) which is a MagicMock \u2014 fine.\n\nBut actually, wait: does DashSegmentsFD's real_download call anything else? `self.report_retry_fragment(err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries)` \u2014 real implementation:\n\n```python\ndef report_retry_fragment(self, err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries):\n    self.to_screen('[download] Got error HTTP error %s ... Retrying (attempt %d of %s) ...' % (...))\n```\n\nFine with MagicMock ydl.\n\n`report_skip_fragment`:\n```python\ndef report_skip_fragment(self, frag_index):\n    self.to_screen('[download] Skipping fragment %d ...' % frag_index)\n```\n\nFine.\n\n`report_error` \u2014 this is the dangerous one. In FileDownloader:\n\n```python\ndef report_error(self, message, tb=None, expected=False):\n    self.ydl.report_error(message, tb, expected)\n```\n\nHmm, or does it call self.trouble? Let me check. In youtube_dl/downloader/common.py:\n\n```python\ndef report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n    \"\"\"Like report_warning but fail the download\"\"\"\n    self.ydl.report_error(msg, tb, expected)\n```\n\nHmm, I'm not sure whether it's in common.py or FileDownloader. If it calls self.ydl.report_error with a MagicMock ydl, it just records the call and doesn't raise. That's actually convenient \u2014 but to be deterministic, I'll mock report_error on the fd instance anyway.\n\nActually wait \u2014 if report_error calls self.ydl.report_error and ydl is a MagicMock, then no exception is raised, and real_download returns False. Good. But I'll mock it to capture the message for assertions.\n\nLet me now check the actual source with get_info to be safe. I'll query:\n- 'DashSegmentsFD' (class info)\n- 'FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD._download_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._append_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._finish_frag_download'\n- 'FileDownloader.report_error'\n- 'FileDownloader.__init__'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_skip_fragment'\n\nLet me make these calls in parallel.\n\nActually, the get_info tool returns \"information about a symbol\" \u2014 presumably source code or signature. Let me call it for the key ones.\n\nThen write the test file.\n\nOne more consideration: the ctx dict. real_download creates ctx with 'filename' and 'total_frags', then calls _prepare_and_start_frag_download(ctx). My mocked prepare sets ctx['fragment_index']. In the real code, _prepare_frag_download does:\n\n```python\nctx.update({\n    'tmpfilename': ...,\n    'fragment_index': 0,\n    ...\n})\n```\n\nActually I recall in FragmentFD._prepare_frag_download:\n\n```python\ndef _prepare_frag_download(self, ctx):\n    if 'live' not in ctx:\n        ctx['live'] = False\n    if not ctx['live'] and (not ctx['tmpfilename'] ...):\n    ...\n    ctx.update({\n        'downloaded_bytes': 0,\n        'frag_index': 0,  # hmm\n        'fragment_index': 0,\n        ...\n    })\n```\n\nWhatever \u2014 since I mock it, I control it. The key: line 36 reads ctx['fragment_index'], so my mock must set it (or the real one would). For tests where I don't care, setting fragment_index=0 in the mock prepare is the right simulation.\n\nLet me also double check `urljoin` from youtube_dl.utils \u2014 it's compat's urljoin (urllib.parse.urljoin). urljoin('http://base/', 'seg1.m4s') = 'http://base/seg1.m4s'. Good.\n\nNow about imports in the test: \n\n```python\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock\nimport pytest\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.dash import DashSegmentsFD\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError\n```\n\nCreating HTTPError: `compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(url, code, msg, hdrs, fp)` \u2014 hdrs and fp can be None. HTTPError is a subclass of URLError and OSError. Constructing with fp=None is fine as long as we don't call .read() etc. The code only passes err to report_retry_fragment. Good.\n\nDownloadError: `DownloadError(msg, exc_info=None)` \u2014 from youtube_dl.utils:\n\n```python\nclass DownloadError(YoutubeDLError):\n    \"\"\"Download Error exception.\n\n    This exception may be thrown by FileDownloader objects if they are not\n    configured to continue on errors. They will just contain a string\n    representation of the exception.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, msg, exc_info=None):\n        \"\"\" exc_info, if given, is the original exception (as from sys.exc_info()), and it is normally more specific than msg.\n        \"\"\"\n        super(DownloadError, self).__init__(msg)\n        self.exc_info = exc_info\n```\n\nGood, DownloadError('boom') works.\n\nNow, the fixture/helper. I'll write a helper function that creates the fd and installs common mocks, returning a recorder object. But instructions say \"Write as little top-level code as possible\" \u2014 helpers are fine, just no top-level execution code (no pytest.main, no direct calls).\n\nLet me design a helper:\n\n```python\nclass Recorder:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.prepared = []\n        self.downloads = []\n        self.appended = []\n        self.finished = []\n        self.retries = []\n        self.skipped = []\n        self.errors = []\n\n\ndef make_fd(monkeypatch, params=None, rec=None, prepare_hook=None, download_fn=None):\n    rec = rec or Recorder()\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), params or {})\n\n    def _prepare(ctx):\n        rec.prepared.append(dict(ctx))\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = 0\n        if prepare_hook:\n            prepare_hook(ctx)\n\n    def _download(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        rec.downloads.append(url)\n        if download_fn is not None:\n            return download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_prepare_and_start_frag_download', _prepare)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', _download)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_append_fragment', lambda ctx, content: rec.appended.append(content))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_finish_frag_download', lambda ctx: rec.finished.append(dict(ctx)))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_retry_fragment', lambda err, fi, count, retries: rec.retries.append((fi, count, retries)))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_skip_fragment', lambda fi: rec.skipped.append(fi))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error', lambda msg, *a, **k: rec.errors.append(msg))\n    return fd, rec\n```\n\nHmm, report_error signature: real one might be `report_error(self, message, tb=None, expected=False)`. My lambda with *a, **k handles it.\n\nWait, one issue: monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error', ...) \u2014 setting an instance attribute on the fd object. monkeypatch will delete it on teardown. Fine.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 is `report_error` defined on FileDownloader or common? If it's not defined on the class, setattr on instance still works (creates instance attr). monkeypatch.setattr requires the attribute to exist by default (raising=False not set). If report_error doesn't exist anywhere in the MRO, monkeypatch.setattr raises AttributeError. Let me verify with get_info that FileDownloader.report_error exists. It should \u2014 FileDownloader has report_error. Let me confirm via get_info.\n\nSimilarly report_retry_fragment and report_skip_fragment are on FragmentFD. _prepare_and_start_frag_download, _download_fragment, _append_fragment, _finish_frag_download on FragmentFD. Let me verify all with get_info.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_success_all_fragments_with_urls(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}, {'url': 'http://e/3'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://e/1', 'http://e/2', 'http://e/3']\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://e/1', b'frag-http://e/2', b'frag-http://e/3']\n    assert rec.finished and not rec.errors and not rec.skipped\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_test_mode_downloads_only_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'test': True})\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://e/1']\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_fragment_without_url_uses_base_url_and_path(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    info_dict = {\n        'fragment_base_url': 'http://base/vid/',\n        'fragments': [{'path': 'init.mp4'}, {'path': 'seg1.m4s'}],\n    }\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://base/vid/init.mp4', 'http://base/vid/seg1.m4s']\n```\n\nurljoin('http://base/vid/', 'init.mp4') \u2192 'http://base/vid/init.mp4'. Good.\n\n```python\ndef test_download_fragment_failure_returns_false(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, download_fn=lambda ctx, url, info: (False, None))\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is False\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://e/1']\n    assert rec.appended == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_retried_then_success(monkeypatch):\n    err = compat_urllib_error.HTTPError('http://e/1', 404, 'Not Found', None, None)\n    state = {'calls': 0}\n\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        state['calls'] += 1\n        if state['calls'] == 1:\n            raise err\n        return True, b'frag'\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 3}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}]}) is True\n    assert state['calls'] == 2\n    assert rec.retries == [(1, 1, 3)]\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag']\n    assert rec.finished and not rec.errors and not rec.skipped\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_exhausted_retries_fatal_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        raise compat_urllib_error.HTTPError('http://e/1', 404, 'Not Found', None, None)\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 1}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}]}) is False\n    assert rec.errors == ['giving up after 1 fragment retries']\n    assert rec.retries == [(1, 1, 1)]\n    assert rec.appended == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n```\n\nTrace: count=0: raise \u2192 count=1, 1<=1 \u2192 report_retry_fragment(1,1,1). count=1: raise \u2192 count=2, 2<=1 false. Exit. count=2>1 \u2192 fatal \u2192 report_error \u2192 return False. retries == [(1,1,1)]. Good.\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_exhausted_retries_skips_unavailable_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        if url == 'http://e/2':\n            raise compat_urllib_error.HTTPError('http://e/2', 500, 'Server Error', None, None)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode()\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 0}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    info = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info) is True\n    assert rec.skipped == [2]\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://e/1']\n    assert rec.finished and not rec.errors\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_http_error_exhausted_retries_no_skip_is_fatal(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        if url == 'http://e/2':\n            raise compat_urllib_error.HTTPError('http://e/2', 500, 'Server Error', None, None)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode()\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 0, 'skip_unavailable_fragments': False}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    info = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info) is False\n    assert rec.errors == ['giving up after 0 fragment retries']\n    assert rec.finished == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_download_error_on_first_fragment_is_fatal(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        raise DownloadError('boom')\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, download_fn=download_fn)\n    with pytest.raises(DownloadError):\n        fd.real_download('out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}]})\n    assert rec.finished == []\n    assert rec.appended == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_download_error_skips_unavailable_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        if url == 'http://e/2':\n            raise DownloadError('boom')\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode()\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, download_fn=download_fn)\n    info = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}, {'url': 'http://e/3'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info) is True\n    assert rec.skipped == [2]\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://e/1', b'frag-http://e/3']\n    assert rec.finished and not rec.errors\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_download_error_no_skip_raises(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info):\n        if url == 'http://e/2':\n            raise DownloadError('boom')\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode()\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'skip_unavailable_fragments': False}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    info = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}]}\n    with pytest.raises(DownloadError):\n        fd.real_download('out.mp4', info)\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://e/1']\n    assert rec.finished == []\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_resume_skips_already_downloaded_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    def prepare_hook(ctx):\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = 2  # first two fragments already present\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, prepare_hook=prepare_hook)\n    info = {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://e/1'}, {'url': 'http://e/2'}, {'url': 'http://e/3'}]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://e/3']\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://e/3']\n    assert rec.finished\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_missing_fragment_url_and_base_url_asserts(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    with pytest.raises(AssertionError):\n        fd.real_download('out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'path': 'seg.m4s'}]})\n    assert rec.downloads == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n```\n\nHmm wait \u2014 in this last test, the AssertionError happens inside the while loop's try. The except clauses don't catch AssertionError, so it propagates out of real_download. Good.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 one subtlety with the assert: if Python is run with -O, asserts are stripped. Tests shouldn't assume -O. Fine.\n\nNow, coverage check \u2014 which lines/branches do these tests hit?\n\nLine 19: fragment_base_url = info_dict.get('fragment_base_url') \u2014 all tests.\nLine 20-21: both branches (test=True in test 2; test=False elsewhere).\nLine 23-25: ctx creation \u2014 all.\nLine 28: _prepare_and_start_frag_download \u2014 all.\nLine 30-31: params.get \u2014 all (various params).\nLine 33-35: loop \u2014 all.\nLine 36-37: continue branch \u2014 test 10 (resume). Non-continue branch \u2014 others.\nLine 40: fatal computation \u2014 both operands: i==0 (many), not skip_unavailable_fragments (tests 8/12).\nLine 41-42: while loop \u2014 all.\nLine 44: fragment.get('url') \u2014 all.\nLine 45-46-47: not fragment_url branch \u2014 tests 3 and 13. With url \u2014 others.\nLine 48: _download_fragment \u2014 all.\nLine 49-50: not success \u2192 return False \u2014 test 4.\nLine 51: _append_fragment \u2014 success tests.\nLine 52: break \u2014 success tests.\nLine 53, 60: HTTPError handler \u2014 tests 5, 6, 7, 8.\nLine 61-62: count <= fragment_retries \u2192 report_retry_fragment \u2014 tests 5, 6. The false branch (count > fragment_retries after increment) \u2014 tests 7, 8 (fragment_retries=0, count becomes 1 > 0).\nLine 63, 66-68: DownloadError handler, not fatal \u2192 skip + break \u2014 test 9. \nLine 69: raise \u2014 tests 8, 10 (DownloadError fatal).\nLine 71: count > fragment_retries \u2014 tests 6, 7, 8. False branch \u2014 others.\nLine 72-74: not fatal \u2192 skip + continue \u2014 test 7.\nLine 75-76: fatal \u2192 report_error + return False \u2014 tests 6, 8.\nLine 78: _finish_frag_download \u2014 success tests.\nLine 80: return True \u2014 success tests.\n\nBranch coverage:\n- Line 20-21 ternary: both.\n- Line 36: both (resume test vs others).\n- Line 40: fatal True via i==0 (tests 6, 8), fatal True via not skip (tests 8-no-skip, 12), fatal False (tests 7, 9).\n- Line 45: both.\n- Line 49: both.\n- Line 52 break / loop continues.\n- Line 61: both (test 5/6 true; test 7/8 false).\n- Line 66: both (test 9 true; tests 8/10 false \u2192 raise).\n- Line 71: both.\n- Line 72: both (test 7 true; tests 6/8 false).\n\nGreat, full coverage of lines 19-80 and all branches.\n\nNow, one thing to verify: the exact behavior of `make_fd` \u2014 DashSegmentsFD(ydl, params). Does FileDownloader.__init__ require anything else? Let me check with get_info('FileDownloader.__init__').\n\nAlso need to check: does `DashSegmentsFD` exist with that name, and does `real_download` signature match? The snippet shows `def real_download(self, filename, info_dict)`. Good.\n\nAlso, `FragmentFD` might have `__init__` that takes (ydl, params)? FileDownloader.__init__(self, ydl, params). Let me verify.\n\nAnother consideration: `self.params.get('test', False)` \u2014 params is the dict we pass. Good.\n\nPotential issue: In `make_fd`, I set instance attributes via monkeypatch.setattr(fd, ...). monkeypatch.setattr on an instance attribute that exists (inherited) \u2014 it sets fd.__dict__ entry and on undo, deletes it (since it didn't exist in instance dict before). Actually monkeypatch records (target, name, oldval) where oldval = getattr sentinel... Let me recall: monkeypatch.setattr uses `oldval = getattr(target, name, notset)`; if notset, it marks for deletion on undo. Since these methods exist on the class, getattr returns the bound method, and on undo it will setattr back the bound method on the instance? Hmm, that would leave a bound method as an instance attribute after undo... Actually no: monkeypatch stores oldval and on undo does setattr(target, name, oldval). If oldval was a bound method from the class, it would set it as an instance attribute \u2014 which is functionally equivalent (bound to same instance) but leaves residue on the instance. Since the fd instance is local to each test and garbage collected, no state pollution across tests. Fine.\n\nAlternatively, I could patch the class methods via monkeypatch.setattr(DashSegmentsFD, ...) but instance-level is cleaner per-test.\n\nHmm, actually there's a subtle issue: monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', _download) \u2014 _download is a plain function taking (ctx, url, info_dict). When called as self._download_fragment(ctx, url, info_dict), since it's an instance attribute (not class), Python doesn't bind self \u2014 it calls _download(ctx, url, info_dict). Correct.\n\nNow let me also double check `compat_urllib_error.HTTPError` construction: HTTPError(url, hdrs? no...). Signature: HTTPError(url, code, msg, hdrs, fp). Yes.\n\nOne more: in test 5, `rec.retries == [(1, 1, 3)]` \u2014 report_retry_fragment(err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries) \u2192 my lambda records (fi, count, retries) = (1, 1, 3). Good.\n\nNow, about the ydl MagicMock: FileDownloader.__init__ might do `self.ydl = ydl` and maybe `self.params = params`. Some versions also set `self.report_progress` stuff. MagicMock handles attribute access. But if __init__ calls ydl methods with real logic expectations... unlikely.\n\nWait, actually there might be an issue: FileDownloader.__init__ in youtube_dl:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, ydl, params):\n    \"\"\"Create a FileDownloader object.\"\"\"\n    self.ydl = ydl\n    self._progress_hooks = []\n    self.params = params\n    self._last_progress_update = 0\n    self._interrupted = False\n```\n\nHmm, I think in youtube_dl it's:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, ydl, params):\n    self.ydl = ydl\n    self.params = params\n    self._progress_hooks = []\n```\n\nLet me just check via get_info.\n\nAlso check `FragmentFD.__init__` \u2014 probably not defined.\n\nLet me also confirm `DashSegmentsFD` module path: youtube_dl/downloader/dash.py \u2014 yes, and the class name DashSegmentsFD.\n\nLet me now call get_info for the symbols. I'll batch independent calls:\n\n1. get_info('DashSegmentsFD')\n2. get_info('FragmentFD')\n3. get_info('FileDownloader.__init__')\n4. get_info('FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download')\n5. get_info('FragmentFD._download_fragment')\n6. get_info('FragmentFD._append_fragment')\n7. get_info('FragmentFD._finish_frag_download')\n8. get_info('FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment')\n9. get_info('FragmentFD.report_skip_fragment')\n10. get_info('FileDownloader.report_error')\n\nThat's a lot of calls; maybe I should be selective. The critical ones: FileDownloader.__init__ (constructor requirements), FragmentFD._download_fragment (signature/return), FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download (what ctx keys it sets), FileDownloader.report_error (signature), FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment / report_skip_fragment (existence/signature). _append_fragment and _finish_frag_download existence.\n\nLet me make the calls.\n\nAfter that, write the final test code.\n\nOne more design point: the instructions say \"Always send entire Python test scripts\" and \"Respond ONLY with the Python code enclosed in backticks\". So my final response should be just the code block. But I need to do tool calls first \u2014 the intermediate turns can contain the tool calls. The final answer must be only the code in backticks.\n\nLet me also think about whether `real_download` uses `self.report_error` with extra args: `self.report_error('giving up after %s fragment retries' % fragment_retries)` \u2014 single arg. My lambda: `lambda msg, *a, **k: rec.errors.append(msg)`. Good.\n\nAlso `report_skip_fragment(self, frag_index)` \u2014 single arg.\n\nNow, is there any chance that `_download_fragment` real signature is `(self, ctx, url, info_dict, success=False)`? In FragmentFD:\n\n```python\ndef _download_fragment(self, ctx, frag_url, info_dict, headers=None, request_data=None):\n    ...\n    return success, frag_content\n```\n\nHmm, in newer yt-dlp it's different. In youtube_dl:\n\n```python\ndef _download_fragment(self, ctx, frag_url, info_dict):\n    down = io.BytesIO()\n    ...\n    success = False\n    try:\n        ...\n        success = True\n    ...\n    return success, down.getvalue()\n```\n\nSomething like that. The call in dash.py is `self._download_fragment(ctx, fragment_url, info_dict)` \u2014 3 args. My mock matches.\n\nLet me verify with get_info anyway.\n\nAlso \u2014 `urljoin` import in dash.py: `from youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError, urljoin`. Fine.\n\nEdge: In test 3, fragment_base_url = 'http://base/vid/' and path 'init.mp4' \u2192 urljoin gives 'http://base/vid/init.mp4'. Good.\n\nNow let me also think: should I use `mocker` from pytest-mock instead of monkeypatch? monkeypatch is built-in; I'll use it.\n\nPotential state pollution: none \u2014 no global state modified; instance-level patches die with the instance; monkeypatch undoes everything.\n\nLet me write the final code now, but first run get_info calls.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the Recorder/make_fd helper \u2014 it's a bit heavy. Alternative: a pytest fixture returning a factory. I'll keep a simple module-level helper function + small class. That's fine (\"as little top-level code as possible\" means no top-level execution; class/function definitions are fine).\n\nLet me write it:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock\n\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.dash import DashSegmentsFD\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError\n\n\nclass Recorder(object):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.prepared = []\n        self.downloads = []\n        self.appended = []\n        self.finished = []\n        self.retries = []\n        self.skipped = []\n        self.errors = []\n\n\ndef make_fd(monkeypatch, params=None, download_fn=None, prepare_hook=None):\n    \"\"\"Build a DashSegmentsFD with its fragment-handling helpers replaced by\n    recording fakes, so that only the logic of ``real_download`` runs.\"\"\"\n    rec = Recorder()\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), params if params is not None else {})\n\n    def fake_prepare(ctx):\n        rec.prepared.append(dict(ctx))\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = 0\n        if prepare_hook is not None:\n            prepare_hook(ctx)\n\n    def fake_download(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        rec.downloads.append(url)\n        if download_fn is not None:\n            return download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_prepare_and_start_frag_download', fake_prepare)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', fake_download)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_append_fragment',\n                        lambda ctx, content: rec.appended.append(content))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_finish_frag_download',\n                        lambda ctx: rec.finished.append(dict(ctx)))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_retry_fragment',\n                        lambda err, frag_index, count, retries:\n                        rec.retries.append((frag_index, count, retries)))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_skip_fragment',\n                        lambda frag_index: rec.skipped.append(frag_index))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error',\n                        lambda msg, *args, **kwargs: rec.errors.append(msg))\n    return fd, rec\n```\n\nThen the tests as planned.\n\nWait \u2014 one concern about `monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error', ...)`: if `report_error` is defined on FileDownloader, getattr(fd, 'report_error') works, so setattr is fine.\n\nBut what if `report_error` in this youtube_dl version is actually `FileDownloader.report_error(self, message, tb=None, expected=False)`? My lambda accepts *args/**kwargs. Good.\n\nAnother concern: `DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), {})` \u2014 FileDownloader.__init__ might access params.get(...) or ydl attributes. MagicMock covers ydl. params={} is a real dict. Should be fine.\n\nHmm, one more potential gotcha: FileDownloader.__init__ might call `self.to_screen` or set up `self._progress_hooks`. Fine.\n\nLet me now also double-check the HTTPError retry test with fragment_retries=3: \n- count=0: try \u2192 raise \u2192 count=1; 1<=3 \u2192 report_retry(err, 1, 1, 3).\n- count=1: try \u2192 success \u2192 break.\nSo retries == [(1, 1, 3)], calls == 2. Good.\n\nAnd test 6 with fragment_retries=1:\n- count=0: raise \u2192 count=1; 1<=1 \u2192 report_retry(err, 1, 1, 1).\n- count=1: raise \u2192 count=2; 2<=1 false.\n- exit loop; count=2 > 1 \u2192 fatal \u2192 report_error('giving up after 1 fragment retries') \u2192 return False.\nretries == [(1, 1, 1)], errors == ['giving up after 1 fragment retries']. Good.\n\nTest 7 with fragment_retries=0, second fragment fails:\n- frag 2: count=0: raise \u2192 count=1; 1<=0 false.\n- exit; count=1 > 0 \u2192 fatal = (i==0)=False or not True=False \u2192 False \u2192 report_skip_fragment(2) \u2192 continue.\n- loop ends; finish; return True.\nskipped == [2]. Good.\n\nTest 12 (no skip, HTTPError exhausted on 2nd fragment): fatal = False or not False = True \u2192 report_error('giving up after 0 fragment retries') \u2192 return False. Good.\n\nTest 9 (DownloadError non-fatal): frag 2 raises DownloadError; fatal=False \u2192 report_skip_fragment(2) \u2192 break; count=0 not > 0 \u2192 continue to frag 3. Good.\n\nTest 10 (DownloadError fatal, first fragment): fatal=True \u2192 raise DownloadError. pytest.raises. Good.\n\nTest 11 (DownloadError, skip_unavailable_fragments=False, second fragment): fatal = False or not False = True \u2192 raise. Good.\n\nTest 13 (resume): prepare_hook sets fragment_index=2. Fragments 1,2 skipped via continue; fragment 3 downloaded. downloads == ['http://e/3']. Good.\n\nTest 14 (assert): fragment {'path': ...} without fragment_base_url \u2192 line 45: fragment_url = None \u2192 not \u2192 assert fragment_base_url \u2192 None \u2192 AssertionError. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 one thing I want to double check: in test 2 (test=True), after downloading the single fragment, `_finish_frag_download` is called and returns True. Yes, the loop ends after 1 fragment.\n\nAlso, in test 2, ctx['total_frags'] == 1. Could assert rec.prepared[0]['total_frags'] == 1. Nice extra assertion. And in test 1, total_frags == 3. Let me add those assertions \u2014 they verify the ctx construction (lines 23-25).\n\nAlso assert rec.prepared[0]['filename'] == 'out.mp4'.\n\nNow, let me run get_info to verify assumptions. I'll batch:\n\n- get_info('DashSegmentsFD')\n- get_info('FileDownloader.__init__')\n- get_info('FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download')\n- get_info('FragmentFD._download_fragment')\n- get_info('FragmentFD._append_fragment')\n- get_info('FragmentFD._finish_frag_download')\n- get_info('FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment')\n- get_info('FragmentFD.report_skip_fragment')\n- get_info('FileDownloader.report_error')\n\nThat's 9 calls. All independent \u2014 batch them in one block.\n\nThen finalize the code.\n\nLet me think about what could differ: maybe `_download_fragment` in this youtube_dl version has signature `(self, ctx, frag_url, info_dict)` and returns `(success, frag_content)`. The dash.py code destructures `success, frag_content = self._download_fragment(ctx, fragment_url, info_dict)`. So my mock returning a 2-tuple is right.\n\nOK, let me make the calls now.\n\nAfter getting info, I'll write the final test script. Let me draft it fully now so I can adjust after the tool results.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for youtube_dl.downloader.dash.DashSegmentsFD.real_download.\n\nThe fragment-handling helpers inherited from FragmentFD are replaced with\nrecording fakes so that the tests exercise exactly the logic of\n``real_download`` (lines 19-80 of dash.py) without any real I/O.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import MagicMock\n\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.dash import DashSegmentsFD\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError\n\n\nclass Recorder(object):\n    \"\"\"Collects the calls made to the patched helper methods.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.prepared = []\n        self.downloads = []\n        self.appended = []\n        self.finished = []\n        self.retries = []\n        self.skipped = []\n        self.errors = []\n\n\ndef make_fd(monkeypatch, params=None, download_fn=None, prepare_hook=None):\n    \"\"\"Create a DashSegmentsFD whose fragment helpers are recording fakes.\"\"\"\n    rec = Recorder()\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(MagicMock(), params if params is not None else {})\n\n    def fake_prepare(ctx):\n        rec.prepared.append(dict(ctx))\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = 0\n        if prepare_hook is not None:\n            prepare_hook(ctx)\n\n    def fake_download(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        rec.downloads.append(url)\n        if download_fn is not None:\n            return download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_prepare_and_start_frag_download', fake_prepare)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', fake_download)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        fd, '_append_fragment', lambda ctx, content: rec.appended.append(content))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        fd, '_finish_frag_download', lambda ctx: rec.finished.append(dict(ctx)))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        fd, 'report_retry_fragment',\n        lambda err, frag_index, count, retries:\n            rec.retries.append((frag_index, count, retries)))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        fd, 'report_skip_fragment',\n        lambda frag_index: rec.skipped.append(frag_index))\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        fd, 'report_error',\n        lambda msg, *args, **kwargs: rec.errors.append(msg))\n    return fd, rec\n\n\ndef http_error(url='http://example.org/x', code=404):\n    return compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(url, code, 'Not Found', None, None)\n\n\ndef test_success_downloads_all_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/3'},\n    ]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == [\n        'http://example.org/1', 'http://example.org/2', 'http://example.org/3']\n    assert rec.appended == [\n        b'frag-http://example.org/1',\n        b'frag-http://example.org/2',\n        b'frag-http://example.org/3']\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n    assert rec.errors == []\n    assert rec.skipped == []\n    assert rec.prepared[0]['filename'] == 'out.mp4'\n    assert rec.prepared[0]['total_frags'] == 3\n\n\ndef test_test_mode_downloads_only_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'test': True})\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n    ]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://example.org/1']\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://example.org/1']\n    assert rec.prepared[0]['total_frags'] == 1\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n\n\ndef test_fragment_without_url_joins_base_url_and_path(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    info_dict = {\n        'fragment_base_url': 'http://example.org/media/',\n        'fragments': [{'path': 'init.mp4'}, {'path': 'seg-1.m4s'}],\n    }\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.downloads == [\n        'http://example.org/media/init.mp4',\n        'http://example.org/media/seg-1.m4s']\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n\n\ndef test_fragment_without_url_and_without_base_url_asserts(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    with pytest.raises(AssertionError):\n        fd.real_download('out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'path': 'seg-1.m4s'}]})\n    assert rec.downloads == []\n    assert rec.appended == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n\n\ndef test_unsuccessful_fragment_download_aborts(monkeypatch):\n    fd, rec = make_fd(\n        monkeypatch, download_fn=lambda ctx, url, info_dict: (False, None))\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n    ]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is False\n    assert rec.downloads == ['http://example.org/1']\n    assert rec.appended == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n\n\ndef test_http_error_is_retried_until_success(monkeypatch):\n    err = http_error()\n    state = {'attempts': 0}\n\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        state['attempts'] += 1\n        if state['attempts'] == 1:\n            raise err\n        return True, b'frag'\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(\n        monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 3}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    assert fd.real_download(\n        'out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://example.org/1'}]}) is True\n    assert state['attempts'] == 2\n    assert rec.retries == [(1, 1, 3)]\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag']\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n    assert rec.errors == []\n\n\ndef test_http_error_exhausts_retries_on_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        raise http_error()\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(\n        monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 1}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    assert fd.real_download(\n        'out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://example.org/1'}]}) is False\n    assert rec.retries == [(1, 1, 1)]\n    assert rec.errors == ['giving up after 1 fragment retries']\n    assert rec.appended == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n\n\ndef test_http_error_exhausts_retries_skips_unavailable_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        if url == 'http://example.org/2':\n            raise http_error(url, 500)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(\n        monkeypatch, params={'fragment_retries': 0}, download_fn=download_fn)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/3'},\n    ]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.skipped == [2]\n    assert rec.appended == [\n        b'frag-http://example.org/1', b'frag-http://example.org/3']\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n    assert rec.errors == []\n\n\ndef test_http_error_exhausts_retries_fatal_when_skipping_disabled(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        if url == 'http://example.org/2':\n            raise http_error(url, 500)\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(\n        monkeypatch,\n        params={'fragment_retries': 0, 'skip_unavailable_fragments': False},\n        download_fn=download_fn)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n    ]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is False\n    assert rec.errors == ['giving up after 0 fragment retries']\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://example.org/1']\n    assert rec.finished == []\n\n\ndef test_download_error_on_first_fragment_is_fatal(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        raise DownloadError('boom')\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, download_fn=download_fn)\n    with pytest.raises(DownloadError):\n        fd.real_download(\n            'out.mp4', {'fragments': [{'url': 'http://example.org/1'}]})\n    assert rec.appended == []\n    assert rec.finished == []\n\n\ndef test_download_error_skips_unavailable_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        if url == 'http://example.org/2':\n            raise DownloadError('boom')\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, download_fn=download_fn)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/3'},\n    ]}\n    assert fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict) is True\n    assert rec.skipped == [2]\n    assert rec.appended == [\n        b'frag-http://example.org/1', b'frag-http://example.org/3']\n    assert len(rec.finished) == 1\n    assert rec.errors == []\n\n\ndef test_download_error_fatal_when_skipping_disabled(monkeypatch):\n    def download_fn(ctx, url, info_dict):\n        if url == 'http://example.org/2':\n            raise DownloadError('boom')\n        return True, b'frag-' + url.encode('utf-8')\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(\n        monkeypatch, params={'skip_unavailable_fragments': False},\n        download_fn=download_fn)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'},\n    ]}\n    with pytest.raises(DownloadError):\n        fd.real_download('out.mp4', info_dict)\n    assert rec.appended == [b'frag-http://example.org/1']\n    assert rec.finished == []\n\n\ndef test_resume_skips_already_downloaded_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    def prepare_hook(ctx):\n        # Simulate a resume: the first two fragments are already on disk.\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = 2\n\n    fd, rec = make_fd(monkeypatch, prepare_hook=prepare_hook)\n    info_dict = {'fragments': [\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/1'},\n        {'url': 'http://example.org/2'}